.Dd October 10, 2026
.Dt BSDPOWER 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm BSDPower
.Nd system.Power capability provider
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the
.Dq system.Power
capability provider: the trusted broker for ACPI power management.
A holder of a system.Power channel queries the supported sleep states or, when
policy permits, requests the machine enter one, instead of driving
.Pa /dev/acpi
directly.
Clients use
.Xr libpowercmp 3 .
Reboot and halt stay with
.Xr capsule 8 ;
.Nm
owns sleep.
.Pp
.Nm
is
.Em born in capability mode :
switchboard execs it already inside the Capsicum cage.
It reaches
.Dv ACPIIO_REQSLPSTATE
only through a
.Pa /dev/acpi
descriptor that switchboard delivered and that
.Nm
narrows with
.Xr cap_ioctls_limit 2
to that single ioctl, so the sandbox exposes exactly the one privileged
operation and nothing else.
It is launched by
.Xr switchboard 8
as the
.Pa /Capabilities/System/Power.cap
bundle and never started by hand.
One bounded kqueue loop serves up to
64 sessions, with at most four sessions per exact client label.
Non-inhibiting sessions expire after 30 seconds without a request.
Active inhibitors remain until release or disconnect and decline idle quiesce.
An explicit supervisor stop still revokes them.
Suspend checks and inhibitor acquisition are serialized in this loop.
.Sh POLICY
Querying the supported sleep states is unprivileged and allowed to every holder.
Suspending is
.Em default-deny :
a label may put the machine to sleep only if
.Pa Config/power.conf
grants it.
The file is UCL:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
default { suspend = false; inhibit = false; }
clients {
	"org.5bsd.powerd" { suspend = true; }
	"org.example.updater" { inhibit = true; }
}
.Ed
.Pp
A label matches by exact string; an unlisted label falls back to
.Va default .
A missing or malformed
.Pa power.conf
is fail-soft: the built-in default-deny stands.
An unexpected suspend is a denial of service, so grant
.Va suspend
only to a trusted power manager.
.Sh SUSPEND INHIBITORS
The separate default-deny
.Va inhibit
permission authorizes one suspend inhibitor per session.
It does not grant suspend authority.
An acknowledged inhibitor makes suspend return EBUSY until it is released
or its owning session disconnects.
Inhibitors are reclaimed on client death
and do not survive provider restart.
No request can release another
session's inhibitor.
Grant inhibition only to trusted clients; holding an
inhibitor indefinitely prevents all BSDPower suspend requests.
These leases do not govern reboot, halt or other kernel suspend paths.
.Pp
Admission and session-failure counters use the shared libservice health
accounting and are logged when the provider exits its session loop.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libpowercmp 3 ,
.Xr acpi 4 ,
.Xr acpiconf 8 ,
.Xr switchboard 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Kory Heard
